Hi [Client Name],<br><br>
A quick update on the TSX following Thursday''s strong session and Friday''s flat open.<br><br>
Thursday''s 248-point gain was driven primarily by financials and utilities responding to easing U.S. Treasury yields, not by a fundamental change in the Hormuz supply situation. The same diplomatic optimism that lifted yields also softened oil prices, which is why energy names are under modest pressure Friday and the index is opening flat.<br><br>
This is the third time we have seen this pattern since the April 8 ceasefire. Oil pulls back on a diplomatic statement, the TSX dips, then the physical supply floor reasserts and oil partially recovers. The TSX at 34,410 is 6.9% above its March 9 low. That recovery has been earned. The question for the weeks ahead is which Hormuz scenario the market prices from here. I will be in touch as that picture develops.<br><br>
