If you watched the TSX this week, you saw something that might have felt contradictory. Thursday was one of the strongest sessions in months. Friday opened flat despite what looked like encouraging news on the U.S.-Iran talks. The reason is worth understanding because it tells you something important about how the TSX is being driven right now.<br><br>
Thursday''s gain was led by financials and utilities responding to easing bond yields, not by the energy sector. The same diplomatic optimism that eased yields also softened oil prices, which is now putting modest pressure on energy names Friday. Two sectors, two transmission mechanisms, same underlying driver.<br><br>
